language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Assign aircraft of several types to several routes: meet the passenger demand of each route, stay within the availability of each aircraft type, and minimise the total operational cost.
given capabilities_dim1, capabilities_dim2 : int(1..)
given availability : matrix indexed by [int(1..capabilities_dim1)] of int(0..)
given demand : matrix indexed by [int(1..capabilities_dim2)] of int(0..)
given capabilities : matrix indexed by [int(1..capabilities_dim1), int(1..capabilities_dim2)] of int(0..)
given costs : matrix indexed by [int(1..capabilities_dim1), int(1..capabilities_dim2)] of int(0..)
find allocation : matrix indexed by [int(1..capabilities_dim1), int(1..capabilities_dim2)] of int(0..sum(availability))

minimising (sum i : int(1..capabilities_dim1) . (sum j : int(1..capabilities_dim2) . costs[i,j] * allocation[i,j]))
such that
$ each route must receive at least its passenger demand in seats from all aircraft assigned to it
forAll j : int(1..capabilities_dim2) . (sum i : int(1..capabilities_dim1) . capabilities[i,j] * allocation[i,j]) >= demand[j],
$ each aircraft type can be assigned at most its available number of aircraft, over all routes
forAll i : int(1..capabilities_dim1) . (sum j : int(1..capabilities_dim2) . allocation[i,j]) <= availability[i]
